Intermediate &
Advanced Roles
Each role is marked by a complexity indicator. When playing with less experienced players, you should stick with basic roles. Intermediate and advanced roles can be added if all players are familiar with the game. There are also some cards that don't have defined abilities: these allow you to customize the game to your wishes.
Basic: The simplest roles that can be used with newer players. Their mechanics are relatively easy for both the players and the Host.
Intermediate: Roles with slightly trickier mechanics such as role changes and day abilities, as well as solo roles (see more on that in the following pages).
Advanced: The most complex roles. These might prove challenging for both players and Hosts and should only be used by experienced players.
None: These roles don't have a specific behaviour defined. The Host and players may agree on rules for these roles.
